  "notes": "West leads the ♥Q against 6♠. West's heart lead is won by South. A top trump is cashed. When West discards, South will have to arrange for a trump endplay against East.\n\nA diamond is played to dummy and a heart is ruffed. South crosses again in diamonds, noting the fall of West's ♦J. Dummy's last heart is ruffed. South's spade length is reduced to that of East.\n\nSouth cashes the ♦Q. West discards confirming the diamond count. East must now be 4342 for the contract to have a chance. South cashes a top club and crosses to dummy in clubs. Dummy's fourth diamond is cashed as South discards his last club.\n\nA club is led from dummy. East will ruff low and South underruffs. East must lead away from the ♠Q at trick 12. If West had followed to the third diamond, South would have to cash 3 rounds of clubs, ending in the dummy. The thirteenth diamond will endplay East in trumps as before.",
  "commentary_paragraphs": [
    "West leads the ♥Q against 6♠. West's heart lead is won by South. A top trump is cashed. When West discards, South will have to arrange for a trump endplay against East.",
    "A diamond is played to dummy and a heart is ruffed. South crosses again in diamonds, noting the fall of West's ♦J. Dummy's last heart is ruffed. South's spade length is reduced to that of East.",
    "South cashes the ♦Q. West discards confirming the diamond count. East must now be 4342 for the contract to have a chance. South cashes a top club and crosses to dummy in clubs. Dummy's fourth diamond is cashed as South discards his last club.",
    "A club is led from dummy. East will ruff low and South underruffs. East must lead away from the ♠Q at trick 12. If West had followed to the third diamond, South would have to cash 3 rounds of clubs, ending in the dummy. The thirteenth diamond will endplay East in trumps as before."
